addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>THE FURUKAWA ELECTRIC CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AIKIYO TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEGAMI YOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIMURA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIKIYO, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEGAMI, YOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A getter housing (10) is formed of a sintered metallic fiber sheet (16) having pores that pass impurity gas but block getter (18) so as to use getter (18) to adsorb or absorb moisture and impurity gas, etc., in the container. Preferably, the sintered metallic fiber sheet (16) is of stainless steel, and the average diameter of the pores is less than 10  mu m, for instance. A getter assembly comprising such a getter (18) and a getter housing (10) is accommodated in an optical device/electric circuit enclosure that encloses an electric circuit and an optical device including a semiconductor laser, for instance, used for an optical relay.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette enceinte à piégeur (10) est faite d'une feuille en fibres métalliques frittées (16) présentant des pores qui laissent passer les gaz d'impuretés, mais arrêtent le piégeur (18) de façon à utiliser le piégeur pour l'adsorption ou l'absorption de l'humidité et des gaz d'impureté, notamment, dans le récipient. De préférence, la feuille en fibres métalliques frittées (16) est faite d'acier inoxydable, le diamètre moyen des pores étant inférieur à 10  mu m notamment. Un ensemble piégeur comprenant un tel piégeur (18) et une enceinte piégeur (10) est reçu dans un dispositif optique ou une enceinte de circuit électrique qui renferme un circuit électrique et un dispositif optique comprenant un laser à semi-conducteur tel que ceux que l'on utilise notamment dans le cas des relais optiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>